Adds informative references to draft-mcguinness-oauth-actor-receipts and draft-mcguinness-oauth-actor-proofs at the three places the spec previously pointed at unspecified evidence:

- the `act` claim's separately retained audit evidence for the offline segment, now with explicit guidance that such evidence stays in the control plane and out of data-plane tokens (consistent with Privacy Considerations);
- the "verifiable delegation artifact" of Chain-Context Provenance item 4;
- the deployment audit records where intermediate workloads outside the authenticated lineage appear.

No normative dependency is introduced; the continuation profile stands alone, and the receipts/proofs drafts slot in as an optional evidence layer. Builds cleanly; references resolve from the datatracker.

Adds an informative reference to draft-li-oauth-delegated-authorization at the three places this document previously described the "offline attenuated delegation token" abstractly:

- the decision rule's local fan-out branch;
- the Envelope Enforcement and Offline Attenuation security subsection (with "parent-hash linkage" generalized to "parent linkage", since the cited stack uses key-continuity rather than hash linkage);
- Appendix A.3, where a sentence notes that its client-issued tokens are forbidden to carry a subject at all — corroborating the mint-not-attenuation boundary from the other side and composing with this profile as the intra-domain layer.

Fills the concrete-mechanism gap left when the unverifiable offline-stack citation was removed. No normative dependency; the reference resolves on the datatracker. Builds with zero warnings.
